# local.properties — gitignored, per-machine. NONE of this is required for the
# demo: the app defaults its helper host to http://localhost:8091, and Android
# Studio writes `sdk.dir` for you. Copy a line below into your real
# `local.properties` (gitignored) ONLY if you need to override a default.

# Android SDK location. Android Studio auto-generates this on first open, so you
# usually never set it by hand. If you build from the CLI without Studio, point
# it at your SDK (or set the ANDROID_HOME / ANDROID_SDK_ROOT env var instead):
# sdk.dir=/absolute/path/to/Android/sdk

# Helper host the TV app talks to. Optional — defaults to http://localhost:8091
# (a locally-run helper, the demo path). Set it to your helper's LAN URL to point
# a device/emulator at a real helper. Resolution order: a -P gradle property >
# this local.properties value > the localhost default. No topology is committed.
#   - emulator → host's localhost is 10.0.2.2:  http://10.0.2.2:8091
#   - real device on the same Wi-Fi:             http://<your-machine-LAN-ip>:8091
#   - an HTTPS helper:                           https://<helper-host>:8443
# MYMTS_HELPER_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8091

# NOTE: release SIGNING is configured separately in app/keystore.properties
# (see app/keystore.properties.example) — debug builds (installDebug, the
# collaborator path) need no signing config and no entry here.
